diagram 1
type flow

graph soccer-coach-access "Sign in to the team workspace"
description "Production coach access through /login. Local development can use a development coach without this sign-in flow."

node coach actor "Coach" layout=0,0
node credentials input "Coach credentials" body="Use the username and private password supplied by the administrator. Account setup is outside this flow." layout=1,0
node sign-in process "Submit sign-in" body="Enter credentials at /login and select Sign in." layout=2,0
node session handoff "Authenticated session" body="Successful authentication permits access to the shared team workspace." layout=3,0
node open-workspace process "Open the requested page" body="Return to the requested route, or open the dashboard when no next route is supplied." layout=4,0
node workspace deliverable "Team workspace access" body="Authorized coaches use the same team records. Administrators manage coach accounts outside this flow." layout=5,0
node resolve-error process "Resolve sign-in failure" body="Correct rejected credentials and submit again. Configuration failures require administrator action before retrying." layout=3,1
node recovery deliverable "Sign-in recovery guidance" body="The error remains visible on the sign-in page. No authenticated access is granted by this path." layout=4,1
node privacy need "Keep team access private"
node feedback ux "Explain sign-in failures" body="Show pending state, credential errors, and service configuration errors. Disable submission when credentials are empty."

edge coach-provides coach -> credentials
edge credentials-to-login credentials -> sign-in
edge login-succeeds sign-in -> session label="Accepted" emphasis=true
edge session-to-page session -> open-workspace
edge page-to-access open-workspace -> workspace
edge login-fails sign-in -> resolve-error label="Rejected or unavailable"
edge failure-to-guidance resolve-error -> recovery
edge session-protects session -> privacy relation=addresses
edge feedback-at-login feedback -> sign-in relation=appears-at
edge feedback-supports feedback -> privacy relation=supports
